Transcript:
- U1: 今実機で起動しているがwaiting sourceのまま、なんで？
  - A: Applied investigate-problem and inspected the live target read-only. Confirmed the Scorepeek listener existed and the layer was loaded into bm2dx.exe, but /run/user/1000/scorepeek was absent from the Pressure Vessel mount namespace. Concluded the fixed runtime socket was unreachable from the game and no producer admission could occur; no live state was changed.
- U2: 設定は？
  - A: Provided the exact launch setting PRESSURE_VESSEL_FILESYSTEMS_RW=/run/user/1000/scorepeek, explained colon-separated composition with any existing value, and noted that the game must be restarted while Scorepeek may remain running.
- U3: activeになったがscreen認識すら動いてないぞ
  - A: Read the latest structured diagnostics and live process path. Admission and 1920x1080 BGRx DMA-BUF import succeeded, consumer requests were consumed, but frame summaries remained count=0 with no READY or typed error. Correlated the loaded DXVK swapchain-maintenance implementation with the layer branch that dropped every present already carrying VkSwapchainPresentFenceInfoEXT. Identified both the application-fence incompatibility and the diagnostic blind spot where counters were only delivered after a successful READY.
- U4: 修正して
  - A: Treated the fix as durable and applied develop-repository plus design-program-observability. Protocol v4 adds per-request STATUS packets so requests, captures, busy drops, and coalesced drops remain observable before the first frame; Rust merges cumulative counters monotonically across STATUS, READY, and ERROR and retains READY counters when readback fails. The layer now borrows a nonexternal application-owned present fence without resetting or destroying it, intercepts reset/destroy/import transitions under the resource lock, preserves completion evidence for queue operations enqueued despite present errors, and fails capture closed for export-capable or imported fence payloads and for metadata tracking failure. Pressure Vessel activation and fence ownership contracts were added to living docs, and the live gate now asserts the Vulkan-specific performance summary and positive capture count. Focused tests exposed and fixed an incomplete Rust packet encoder and asynchronous counter-test oracle. Multiple fresh read-only reviews found and drove fixes for enqueued-error semaphore lifetime, stale STATUS/READY counter ordering, ERROR/readback counter loss, external fence payload replacement, and metadata fail-open behavior; the final fresh review reported no actionable findings. Final mise run test passed, and capture:vulkan:test:live passed with vkcube, Gamescope, obs-vkcapture coexistence, real normalized frames, and Scorepeek reconnection. Committed as 1cf301f and rebuilt target/debug/scorepeek plus the Vulkan layer from committed source. The initial post-commit build was blocked only by sandbox denial of the mise task-source cache and succeeded with approved target-equivalent permission. No push or target deployment was performed; bm2dx.exe validation remains the user-owned final check.
